    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189533": {
      "title": "Neuropsychologist, Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Neurology, Neuropsychology",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Neurology Location: Stony Brook, New York Position Summary: Direct clinical neuropsychological services. Duties of a Neuropsychologist may include the following but are not limited to: Administration, scoring, interpretation of neuropsychological assessment measures, cognitive remediation. Report writing based on above. Involvement in multidisciplinary teams. Interviewing and consultation with patients and families. Possible involvement in psychotherapy and/or family support groups as related to neurological and neuropsychiatric disorders (e.g., concussion, epilepsy, ADHD). Participation in departmentally based research programs. Supervision of graduate students in psychology. Supervision of postdoctoral fellows. Required Qualifications: Completion of PhD, PsyD (or foreign equivalent) in psychology (Accreditation through the American Psychological Association preferred) Completion or in the process of completing a neuropsychology fellowship Licensed to practice psychology in New York state Primary training in either pediatric or lifespan neuropsychology Eligibility for board certification through the American Board of Clinical Neuropsychology or the American Board of Neuropsychology Preferred Qualifications: Experience treating patients with neurological disorders. Experience using EMR. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Jamie Friede at 631-444-8397. Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County.  With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192241": {
      "title": "Psychologist, Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Neurology, Outpatient",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Neurology Location: Stony Brook, New York We are seeking a skilled and compassionate generalist clinical psychologist for our expanding Neurology services across Suffolk County who will welcome the challenge and satisfaction of providing behavioral health care to a diverse pediatric and adult populations with neurological disorders. The role of the clinical psychologist will be integrated into collaboration with a motivated group of clinicians, researchers and educators. This position offers the opportunity to work closely with neurologists and psychiatrists who will provide medical management alongside therapy, as well as allied health professionals to deliver comprehensive, patient-centered care for pediatric and adult patients living with chronic neurological conditions. The therapy services provided will be tailored to individuals with neurological disorders in the areas of epilepsy, cerebrovascular, neuromuscular, movement, memory, and behavioral-developmental disorders. The psychologists will be expected to provide one-time consultations, individual or group therapies ranging from short-term goal oriented/solution-focused treatments, to evidence-based practices for more chronic mental health presentations/concerns. Developing integrated care plans, offering counseling, psychoeducation for patients and families adjusting to new diagnoses or disease progression, as well as providing behavioral management strategies for children and adults with chronic neurological disorders will be central to the role of the psychologist. Majority of patient appointments and therapy sessions will be scheduled via telehealth, in-person appointments and therapy sessions can be accommodated as needed. The psychologist may be asked to teach, supervise, or mentor medical students, post doc fellows, residents in Neurology, Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuropsychology. There are also opportunities for clinical research alongside neuroscientists with appointments at Stony Brook Medicine and Stony Brook University. Required Qualifications: PsyD or PhD (or foreign equivalent) in Clinical Psychology from an APA-accredited program or PCSAS-accredited program.  Experience in evidence-based treatment modalities. New York State Clinical Psychologist license or eligibility. Must have passed EPPP for licensure eligibility and will complete all post-doctoral clinical hours prior to start date. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical experience and/or training in treating complex chronic illness across the lifespan including intellectual/developmental disabilities, geriatric mood disorders, Tourette’s syndrome, Huntington’s disease, somatoform disorders and deep brain stimulation surgery. Clinical experience with time-limited goal-oriented therapies, including cognitive behavioral therapy and short-term psychodynamic/relational and attachment-based therapies; experience with cognitive behavioral intervention for tics (CBIT). Mental Health interventions in the setting of interdisciplinary care. A track record of education and research. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Jamie Friede at 631-444-8397. Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192242": {
      "title": "Neurologist - Movement Disorders, Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Neurology, Movement Disorders",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Neurology Location: Stony Brook, New York The Department of Neurology in the Renaissance School of Medicine is seeking movement disorders neurologists to join our outstanding Stony Brook Parkinson's and Movement Disorders Center. Stony Brook is home to the only deep brain stimulation surgical program, TAA Center of Excellence for Tourette syndrome and Tic Disorders, HDSA Center of Excellence for Huntington's disease in Suffolk County, Long Island, NY. Suffolk County has a catchment area of 1.5 million residents, of which nearly a quarter of a million are geriatric. We are members of the Parkinson Study and Huntington Study Groups, with active clinical trials and investigator-initiated research. We partner with Stony Brook Southampton Hospital, which offers numerous wellness programs with support from APDA: Center for Parkinson's Disease | Stony Brook Southampton Hospital Stony Brook University Hospital is a 624-bed tertiary care university hospital. Its academic affiliate, Stony Brook University, is ranked #1 among New York state public universities. It has a state-of-the-art PET-MRI and other neuroimaging with a cyclotron. Responsibilities include: Management of patients with Movement Disorders, including inpatient Movement Disorders consultations. Commitment to community engagements and education. Coverage of the general neurology and consult services shared equally among faculty. Favorable weekend and overnight call responsibility shared equally among faculty. Supervision of neurology residents and medical students. This represents an exciting opportunity for a Movement Disorders neurologist interested in building an outpatient movement disorders practice at the region's premier academic medical center. Candidates will have the opportunity to develop innovative clinical, educational and research programs to suit their unique academic interests. Faculty can also take advantage of an exceptional retirement plan offered through the New York State Pension plan and 457(b), 401(a) and 403(b). Required Qualifications: MD, DO degree (or foreign equivalent). Movement Disorders fellowship training. Board Certified/Board Eligible in Neurology. Eligibility for New York State licensure. Preferred Qualifications: Two years or more of fellowship training. Proficiency in DBS programming and botulinum toxin treatment. Experience in DBS intraoperative neurophysiology. Interest in building specialized programs focusing on neurogenetics, ataxia, normal pressure hydrocephalus, or brain bank. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Jamie Friede at 631-444-8397. Special Notes: Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care.  It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Technology and Management, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County.  With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center.  Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research.  Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine.  We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194124": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neurologist, Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Neurology, Pediatric",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Neurology Location: Stony Brook, New York The Department of Neurology at SUNY Stony Brook has full-time pediatric neurology faculty position available on both the clinical and tenure tracks (Assistant or Associate Professor of Neurology).  Responsibilities include clinical care, teaching, and the opportunity to be involved in clinical research activities. Clinical and research opportunities are available in autism, epilepsy, infectious disease, stroke, and MS. Required Qualifications: MD degree (or foreign equivalent). Eligibility for NYS license. Completion of an accredited Pediatric Neurology residency. Candidate must be board certified or board eligible in Pediatric Neurology with special competency in Child Neurology (SCCN). Preferred Qualifications: Fellowship training in Child Neurology and an interest in neuromuscular disorders, neonatal neurology, movement disorders, childhood stroke, neurogenetics/metabolics, sleep disorders are highly desirable. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Jamie Friede at 631-444-8397. Special Notes Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA.  To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Technology and Management, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 603 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194583": {
      "title": "Pediatric Neurosurgeon, Assistant Professor, Neurosurgery, Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Neurosurgery Location: Stony Brook, New York The Department of Neurological Surgery at Stony Brook University seeks a fellowship-trained pediatric neurosurgeon to join an established pediatric neurosurgery service at Stony Brook Children's Hospital, at the rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will partner with a pediatric neurosurgeon to deliver pediatric neurosurgical care for the region. Stony Brook Children's Hospital is the regional referral center for pediatric care in Suffolk County and eastern Long Island, a catchment of approximately 1.5 million people. Stony Brook University Hospital is a Level I trauma center for both adult and pediatric patients. Clinical environment: 46-bed NICU and 10-bed PICU Pediatric epilepsy monitoring unit and multidisciplinary pediatric epilepsy conference, with active SEEG, DBS, and laser interstitial thermal therapy (LITT) programs Complete neuroendoscopy instrumentation Multidisciplinary pediatric neuro-oncology conference with pediatric oncology and radiation oncology Fetal medicine program Multidisciplinary craniofacial team All pediatric medical and surgical subspecialties represented Strong adult neurosurgical subspecialty colleagues in functional, neuroendovascular, spine, neuro-oncology, and skull base surgery, with dedicated neuroendovascular support for pediatric cases Practice: The balance of pediatric and adult elective practice is tailored to the candidate's interests, with the opportunity to build a pediatric subspecialty program and, if desired, an adult subspecialty practice. Call is shared adult and pediatric neurosurgical call. The department's current faculty include eight neurosurgeons, two with pediatric neurosurgical expertise, along with neurointensivists and spine physiatrists. The team is supported by neurosurgical residents and an experienced group of advanced practice providers across inpatient and outpatient care. Academic: ACGME-accredited neurosurgery residency Dedicated departmental research support and multiple active NIH-funded clinical trials Opportunities for collaboration across a major public research university We offer: Competitive compensation with a dedicated call compensation structure Generous New York State (SUNY) benefits, including state retirement options and health plan A collegial, multidisciplinary department Required Qualifications: MD, DO, or foreign equivalent Completion of an ACGME- or RCPSC-accredited neurological surgery residency Board eligible or board certified in neurological surgery by ABNS, AOA, or RCPSC Completion of an ACPNF-accredited pediatric neurosurgery fellowship or equivalent, with eligibility for ABPNS certification Eligible for New York State medical licensure at the time of application; licensed by the start date Preferred Qualifications: PhD or equivalent research training, or a record of scholarly productivity Interest or experience in pediatric and adult spine surgery and neurotrauma All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Donna Pignataro at Donna.Pignataro@stonybrookmedicine.edu Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: August 2027 Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192397": {
      "title": "Maternal Fetal Medicine Specialist, Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor, OBGYN, MFM",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Medicine Location: Stony Brook, New York The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Medicine at Stony Brook Medicine is seeking an Maternal Fetal Medicine specialist to join an existing MFM Division of eight full-time faculty members. Applicants looking to develop an academic career in Maternal Fetal Medicine should apply. Stony Brook University Hospital is a tertiary care center with 4,000 deliveries annually.  The Division of MFM has an ACGME accredited MFM Fellowship with 2 fellows per year. This is a dynamic department with a large clinical volume, modern Women and Infant’s Hospital facilities, and an AIUM accredited state-of-the-art ultrasound unit.  Opportunities for clinical and basic research are expanded by our affiliation with research facilities at Cold Spring Harbor and Brookhaven National Research Laboratories. Required Qualifications: Candidates should have a MD degree (or foreign equivalent), Board certified or eligible in Obstetrics and Gynecology, Board certified or eligible in Maternal Fetal Medicine, and have a New York State license or be eligible for one. Preferred Qualifications: A background in prenatal diagnosis/genetics is preferred. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Rita Bisso at rita.bisso@stonybrookmedicine.edu Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center.  Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
