    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190109": {
      "title": "Developmental/Behavioral Pediatrics or Neurodevelopmental Disabilities Pediatrician, Assistant/Associate Professor, Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Pediatrics Location: Stony Brook, New York The Division of Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics at Stony Brook Children’s Hospital and the Renaissance School of Medicine at Stony Brook University is seeking a full‑time Board‑Certified/Board‑Eligible Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrician or Neurodevelopmental Disabilities Pediatrician at the Assistant or Associate Professor level to join our expanding academic and clinical division. Candidates must possess or be eligible for New York State licensure. About the Division As an academic medical center, Stony Brook offers a rich environment for clinical care, teaching, research, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Faculty members participate actively in medical education across the undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate spectrum. Interest in research, scholarship, and quality improvement is strongly encouraged and well supported. The Division’s current academic and clinical activities include: Research on caregiver and provider perceptions of autism and developmental delay. Validation studies of autism screening tools in young children. Quality improvement initiatives focused on new systems of care. Collaborative projects with Pediatrics (Primary Care, NICU Follow‑Up, Genetics, Neurology), Child Psychiatry, and other departments. Participation in community and school outreach through the Stony Brook Medicine CARE program. Leadership and training within the Stony Brook LEND Program (Leadership Education in Neurodevelopmental Disabilities). Engagement with early childhood stakeholders including Help Me Grow and Early Intervention Programs. The Health Sciences Center and Neuroscience Institute provide exceptional opportunities for clinical and basic science research, with competitive departmental seed funding available for junior and mid‑career investigators. Responsibilities Comprehensive neurodevelopmental and developmental evaluations, diagnosis, and treatment for: Autism Spectrum Disorder, ADHD, Global Developmental Delay, Learning Disorders, Intellectual Disability, Genetic Syndromes, Cerebral Palsy, behavioral concerns, and other developmental/behavioral conditions. Psychopharmacologic management for ADHD and related behavioral needs. Participation in interdisciplinary clinical teams. Teaching of medical students, residents (Pediatrics, Med/Peds, Neurology), fellows, trainees, and community partners. Collaboration on research, quality improvement, and program development initiatives. Clinical Environment Stony Brook Children’s serves nearly 500,000 children across Suffolk County, NY. Key resources include: A dedicated tertiary‑care Long Island Children’s Hospital , opened in 2019 as part of Stony Brook Medicine’s $423 million expansion, including the MART (Medical and Research Translation) building. A robust faculty of 150 pediatric specialists across all major subspecialties. Pediatric, Med/Peds, and Child Neurology residency programs, plus selected subspecialty fellowships. Extensive laboratory, translational, and clinical research infrastructure across 20 clinical departments and the broader university. Compensation & Benefits The State University of New York (SUNY) offers a highly competitive compensation package designed to support long‑term professional growth and well‑being. Benefits include: Comprehensive tuition assistance programs Tax‑deferred savings options. Long‑term and short‑term disability coverage Workers’ compensation and FMLA compliance Generous retirement plans High‑quality health, dental, vision, and life insurance Salary is commensurate with experience and training. The Environs Stony Brook Children’s Hospital is located in one of New York’s most desirable regions, offering an exceptional blend of coastal beauty, cultural richness, and academic excellence. Ten minutes from the beach. One hour by train to New York City. Scenic Suffolk County: beaches, pumpkin patches, lavender fields, Dickens‑themed winter festivals, farmers’ markets, and vibrant local eateries. Outstanding outdoor recreation and family‑friendly activities. Stony Brook University — ranked among the top 1% of universities worldwide — renowned for groundbreaking scientific achievements including identifying the cause of Lyme disease and constructing the first nuclear MRI of a living organism. Easy access to performing arts, athletics, and cultural events. Excellent local schools and a strong sense of community. Stony Brook offers the best of both worlds: peaceful coastal living with immediate access to world‑class urban culture. Application Process Qualified candidates will hold an MD/DO Degree and be Board Eligible or Board Certified in Developmental & Behavioral Pediatrics or Neurodevelopmental Disabilities. Candidates should demonstrate commitment to collaborative clinical care, medical education, and academic development. Preference will be given to candidates who possess experience with developing and conducting research and QI projects. Interested applicants should submit: Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest Required Qualifications : MD/DO Degree (or foreign equivalent). Board Certified/Board Eligible in Developmental/Behavioral Pediatrics or Neurodevelopmental Disabilities. New York State Licensed or eligible. Commitment to collaborative clinical care, medical education and academic development. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with developing and conducting research and QI projects. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Janet DeLuca at janet.deluca@stonybrookmedicine.edu . Special Notes: T enure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190126": {
      "title": "Clinical Geneticist, Assistant/Associate Professor, Pediatrics",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Pediatrics Location: Stony Brook, New York The Division of Medical Genetics, Genomics and Metabolism at Stony Brook Children’s Hospital and the Renaissance School of Medicine at Stony Brook University is seeking a full-time Board Certified/Board Eligible Clinical Geneticist at the Assistant or Associate Professor level to join our growing, diverse, and multidisciplinary team. Candidates must possess or be eligible for New York State medical licensure. Responsibilities and Requirements : The successful candidate will provide comprehensive inpatient and outpatient clinical genetics services to a diverse pediatric and adult patient population. Clinical responsibilities will include the evaluation, diagnosis, counseling, and longitudinal management of patients with suspected or confirmed genetic disorders, including congenital anomalies, neurodevelopmental disorders, hereditary cancer predisposition syndromes, metabolic disorders, and other rare diseases. The position includes participation in inpatient consultations at Stony Brook Children’s Hospital and affiliated clinical facilities, as well as collaboration with pediatric and adult subspecialists across Stony Brook Medicine. The faculty member will work closely with genetic counselors, advanced practice providers, metabolic dietitians, nursing staff, laboratory personnel, and other members of the multidisciplinary genetics team. The Division currently consists of two clinical geneticists, one nurse practitioner, five genetic counselors, one metabolic dietitian, and two administrative support staff.  The successful candidate will join an established and collaborative clinical program with substantial opportunities to help define its next phase of development. The Division is actively expanding the scope and reach of its clinical programs. Strategic priorities include growth in gene therapy and enzyme replacement therapy, as well as the development and expansion of dedicated programs in cardiogenetics, cancer genetics, and neurogenetics. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to contribute to program development, establish multidisciplinary clinical pathways, build partnerships across pediatric and adult specialties, participate in therapeutic implementation and longitudinal treatment programs, and develop an area of clinical focus aligned with the candidate’s expertise and interests. Board certification or board eligibility in Clinical Genetics and Genomics through the American Board of Medical Genetics and Genomics is required. Certification or eligibility in Clinical Biochemical Genetics is desirable but is not required. Candidates with expertise in biochemical genetics may participate in the diagnosis and management of inborn errors of metabolism, enzyme replacement therapy programs, emerging molecular and gene-based therapies, newborn screening follow-up, and the longitudinal care of pediatric and adult patients with metabolic disease. Candidates with additional certification, training, or experience in Laboratory Genetics and Genomics, Clinical Molecular Genetics and Genomics, or molecular diagnostic laboratory medicine are particularly encouraged to apply. Stony Brook Medicine is developing its molecular diagnostic capabilities, and this position offers an opportunity for qualified candidates to participate in the establishment and growth of a clinical molecular genetics laboratory. Depending on the candidate’s background and interests, opportunities may include assay development and validation, test implementation, genomic data interpretation, laboratory quality initiatives, clinical-laboratory integration, and future laboratory leadership. Prior laboratory directorship experience is not required. As an academic institution, this position requires a significant commitment to teaching across the undergraduate and graduate medical education spectrum.  Educational responsibilities may include teaching medical students, residents, fellows, genetic counseling trainees, and other healthcare professionals. Participation in resident and fellow education, interdisciplinary conferences, and departmental educational activities is expected. Interest in clinical research, translational research, scholarship, quality improvement, and program development is strongly encouraged. The successful candidate will have opportunities to develop an academic portfolio aligned with their clinical, educational, laboratory, or research interests. Opportunities exist to participate in clinical trials, natural-history studies, therapeutic registries, investigator-initiated research, and other scholarly activities related to rare disease and genomic medicine. The clinical services of Stony Brook Children’s serve the nearly 500,000 children of Suffolk County, New York, and include the following resources: A dedicated tertiary-care children’s hospital located on Long Island, outside New York City. Stony Brook Children’s opened its new Children’s Hospital in November 2019. This facility is part of Stony Brook Medicine’s $423 million expansion project, which also includes the Medical and Research Translation building. A 10-bed medical-surgical Pediatric Intensive Care Unit featuring large individual rooms, a bariatric room, and capacity for additional step-down beds. A dedicated Pediatric Emergency Department. A Level I Pediatric Trauma Center. A large Department of Pediatrics faculty representing the full range of pediatric subspecialties, including Adolescent Medicine, Allergy and Immunology, Cardiology, Child Abuse and Advocacy, Developmental and Behavioral Pediatrics, Emergency Medicine, Endocrinology, Gastroenterology, Genetics and Genomics, Hematology and Oncology, Hospital Medicine, Infectious Diseases, Neonatology, Nephrology, Neurology, Pulmonology, and Rheumatology. Pediatric, Internal Medicine-Pediatrics, and Child Neurology residency training programs, as well as selected pediatric subspecialty fellowships. Opportunities to participate in the development and delivery of advanced therapeutics, including gene therapy and enzyme replacement therapy, in collaboration with relevant clinical specialties, pharmacy, nursing, infusion services, and institutional research infrastructure. Extensive resources for laboratory, translational, and clinical research within the clinical departments of the Renaissance School of Medicine and the broader Stony Brook University research community. Competitive seed funding may be available within the Department for junior investigators and mid-career investigators pursuing new research directions. Compensation and Benefits: The compensation package is highly competitive. The State University of New York supports tuition assistance programs, tax-deferred savings programs, long-term and short-term disability plans, workers’ compensation, Family and Medical Leave Act benefits, and generous retirement plans. Comprehensive benefit plans include health, dental, vision, and life insurance.  Academic rank and starting salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience, training, qualifications, and scholarly accomplishments. The Environs: Stony Brook Children’s Hospital is approximately a 10-minute drive from the beach and is accessible to New York City by train.  Life in and around Stony Brook offers access to both the natural environment of Long Island and the cultural resources of the New York metropolitan region. Suffolk County offers extensive beaches, parks, outdoor recreation, farmers’ markets, vineyards, seasonal festivals, and a broad range of dining and cultural activities. The museums, performing arts, restaurants, and other cultural institutions of New York City are approximately one hour away. Stony Brook University is ranked among the leading research universities in the United States and internationally. The University has a substantial record of scientific discovery and innovation, including major contributions to biomedical research, imaging, physics, and the study of infectious diseases. Stony Brook University’s performing arts, athletic, educational, and cultural events are readily accessible from the hospital. High-quality local school districts contribute to a family-friendly environment. Application: The successful candidate will possess an MD or DO degree, or an equivalent medical degree, and will be Board Eligible or Board Certified in Clinical Genetics and Genomics through the American Board of Medical Genetics and Genomics. Candidates must possess or be eligible for an unrestricted New York State medical license. Board certification or eligibility in Clinical Biochemical Genetics is desirable but not required. Additional training or certification in Laboratory Genetics and Genomics, Clinical Molecular Genetics and Genomics, or a related molecular diagnostic discipline is considered an important additional qualification. Candidates must demonstrate a commitment to collaborative clinical care, medical education, program development, and professional advancement. Preference will be given to candidates with experience in medical education, multidisciplinary clinical care, clinical or translational research, molecular diagnostics, laboratory development, or scholarly activity. Required Qualifications : MD/DO Degree (or foreign equivalent). Board Certified/Board Eligible in Clinical Genetics and Genomics through the American Board of Medical Genetics or Genomics. Candidates must possess or be eligible for an unrestricted New York State medical license. Preferred Qualifications: Board certification or eligibility in Clinical Biochemical Genetics is desirable but not required.  Additional training or certification in Laboratory Genetics and Genomics, Clinical Molecular Genetics and Genomics, or a related molecular diagnostic discipline is considered an important additional qualification. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Janet DeLuca at janet.deluca@stonybrookmedicine.edu . Special Notes T enure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191709": {
      "title": "Neonatal Nurse Practitioner Leader, Clinical Instructor, Pediatrics, Neonatology",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Pediatrics Location: Stony Brook, New York Neonatal Nurse Practitioner (NNP) Leader Position Summary: The NNP Leader oversees the Neonatal Nurse Practitioner team and supports high-quality, evidence-based care in the neonatal intensive care unit (NICU). This role provides clinical leadership, coordinates staffing and scheduling, facilitates education and professional development, and leads outreach initiatives that strengthen relationships with internal and external partners. The NNP Leader collaborates with medical directors, nursing leadership, and administrative teams to ensure optimal patient outcomes and operational efficiency. Key Responsibilities 1. Leadership & Clinical Oversight Serve as the primary point of contact and leader for the NNP team. Ensure adherence to clinical standards, scope of practice, and regulatory requirements. Support quality improvement initiatives, clinical protocols, and patient-safety programs. Participate in staffing decisions, recruitment, orientation, and performance evaluations for NNP staff. 2. Scheduling & Workforce Management Create, manage, and maintain the NNP schedule to ensure 24/7 coverage consistent with patient-care needs. Monitor clinical workload, staffing patterns, and productivity metrics. Coordinate PTO approval, schedule swaps, and coverage for unplanned absences. Collaborate with leadership on staffing models, FTE allocation, and onboarding plans. 3. Education & Professional Development Develop and lead ongoing education programs for NNPs, including clinical skills, evidence-based practice updates, and new equipment or procedures. Coordinate onboarding, competency validation, and mentorship for new NNPs. Provide continuing education opportunities, journal clubs, simulations, and case reviews. Support NNP participation in conferences, certifications, and advanced training. 4. Outreach & Community/Regional Relations Represent the NNP team in outreach efforts with referring hospitals, transport teams, and community partners. Develop and deliver educational outreach programs for regional clinicians, nurses, and providers. Support collaborative initiatives that improve neonatal stabilization, transport processes, and early referrals. Participate in community events, parent education programs, and hospital-sponsored outreach activities. 5. Administrative & Operational Coordination Assist with policy development, workflow optimization, and integration of best practices. Track and report metrics related to staffing, outcomes, educational activities, and quality initiatives. Support accreditation activities and compliance with state, national, and organizational standards. Serve on relevant committees and interprofessional working groups. Skills & Competencies Strong leadership, team-building, and communication skills. Expertise in neonatal assessment, management, and evidence-based practice. Ability to coordinate complex schedules and manage staffing needs. Skilled educator with experience teaching diverse learners. Strong organizational and project-management skills. Ability to collaborate effectively across disciplines and settings. Required Qualifications: Master's or Doctoral degree in Nursing with a focus in Neonatal Nurse Practitioner Current natiional certification as an NNP State APRN/NNP licensure Minimum 3-5 years of clinical experience as an NNP, preferably in a Level III or IC NICU Preferred Qualifications: Additional coursework or certification in leadership, education, or management Prior leadership, education, or supervisory experience All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Janet DeLuca at janet.deluca@stonybrookmedicine.edu . Special Notes: Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County.  With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187532": {
      "title": "Psychiatrist, Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor, Psychiatry, Child & Adolescent Inpatient Unit (Part-Time/Weekends/Vacation Coverage/Holidays)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Psychiatry and Behavioral Health Location: Stony Brook, New York We are seeking a child and adolescent psychiatrist to join our expanding hospital-based Psychiatry and Behavioral Health services. At Stony Brook University Hospital, we provide comprehensive, evidence-based mental health services across the lifespan, to a diverse population with a wide range of clinical presentations and psychosocial needs. Stony Brook Children’s Hospital is Suffolk County’s only children’s hospital. We have more than 180 pediatric specialists in 40 specialties. The hospital is Suffolk County’s only Level 4 Regional Perinatal Center and Level 1 Regional Pediatric Trauma Center. Ideal candidates will be committed to delivering high-quality, patient-centered, evidence-based care, and having a desire to work collaboratively with a multidisciplinary team and teach child and adolescent psychiatry fellows and other trainees. The Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor will serve as the attending on weekends and planned coverage on vacation and leave for our 10-bed Inpatient Unit for Children & Adolescents (aged 9-15 years old) and will provide psychiatric consultation to patients admitted to Stony Brook Children’s Hospital. Responsibilities include direct patient care involving psychiatric diagnostic evaluations and treatment of on the psychiatric unit with a team consisting of psychologists, behavioral specialists, special education teachers and a school psychologist, social workers, nursing, activities therapists, and fellow and psychiatric consultation and follow up care at the pediatric hospital. This role also involves teaching and supervision of child and adolescent psychiatry fellows. Work Schedule: This is a part-time, 20-hour-per-week position that typically covers weekend Saturday & Sunday shifts. Some flexibility in scheduling is required to meet operational needs, including providing vacation and some Holiday coverage when needed. This may involve working additional weekday hours during a two-week pay period in place of regularly scheduled weekend coverage, based on departmental needs. Further details will be shared during an interview. Required Qualifications: Child and Adolescent Psychiatrist MD/DO (or foreign equivalent). Board Eligibility or Board Certification required in Child and Adolescent Psychiatry. New York State license at start date. Preferred Qualifications: Inpatient Child & Adolescent Experience. Experience in teaching A track record of academic accomplishment. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807 For questions regarding this position, please contact Michele Chituk at Michele.Chituk@stonybrookmedicine.edu Special Notes: Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190384": {
      "title": "Interventional Psychiatrist, Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor, Psychiatry, Adult Outpatient (OPD)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Psychiatry and Behavioral Health Location: Stony Brook, New York Stony Brook University Department of Psychiatry is undergoing tremendous growth. Our adult outpatient psychiatry service is expanding and we are looking for individuals who welcome the challenge and satisfaction of providing outpatient psychiatric care to a diverse population win collaboration with a motivated group of clinicians, educators and researchers. The Clinical Assistant Professor of Interventional Psychiatry will serve as an Attending Psychiatrist in the Treatment Refractory Depression (TRD) Program in Adult Outpatient Psychiatry. The attending psychiatrist will perform evaluations and treatment of patients with Treatment Resistant Depression (TRD) for/with advanced antidepressant therapies such as Pharmacotherapy, Psychotherapy, Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation (TMS), Ketamine Intra Nasal or Intra Venous Therapy (KINT or KIVT), Electro Convulsive Therapy (ECT), Vagus Nerve Stimulation (VNS), as well as other advanced antidepressant treatment modalities. Responsibilities include direct patient care in the adult outpatient clinic, including diagnostic evaluations, follow-up care, telepsychiatry and teaching and supervision of medical students, residents and fellows. Research, teaching and clinical supervision of psychiatric residents and medical students and other trainees are integral parts of this position, along with direct involvement in process improvement and program development. We are a fast growing program and service which adheres to the consultation model of service delivery and are looking to further impact the health of the population we serve through the addition of new therapies. Shifts totaling 40 hours per week (with hospital weekend/holiday on call, if needed). There are also opportunities for clinical research involving psychiatric inpatient and outpatient treatment and in collaboration with other departments. Required Qualifications: M.D./D.O. (or foreign eqivalent) with Board Eligibility or Board Certification in Adult Psychiatry. Eligibility for New York State licensure. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical experience in an Adult Psychiatry Outpatient Program. Experience in transcranial magnetic brain stimulation. Track record of research/teaching experience in Psychiatry. Experience with treating patients with Ketamine and TMS All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Michelle Chituk at michelle.chituk@stonybrookmedicine.edu. Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193959": {
      "title": "Social Worker (LCSW), Clinical Instructor, Psychiatry, Adult Outpatient (OPD)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Psychiatry and Behavioral Health Location: Stony Brook, New York Our adult outpatient psychiatry service is expanding, and we are looking for a clinical social worker (LCSW) who welcomes the challenge and satisfaction of providing behavioral health care to a diverse population in collaboration with a motivated group of clinicians, researchers, and educators. Our social workers provide clinical services and may also contribute to academic activities such as teaching, providing supervision and research. The clinician will serve as a Clinical Social Worker in our adult outpatient clinic located in the newly renovated Putnam Hall on the South Campus of Stony Brook University and may include integration with medical subspecialty areas. Responsibilities include direct patient care including needs assessments, diagnostic evaluations, individual and group psychotherapy. Clinical Social Workers with experience treating substance use disorders and/or experience with treating clinically complex symptoms and presentations are encouraged to apply. FLEXIBLE: Full-Time schedule totaling forty hours 5 days per week, including the possibility of evening hours; hybrid work schedule including appointments via telehealth. *Please note: The telehealth policy could be subject to change by Stony Brook University and Stony Brook Hospital if needed. Per Stony Brook Hospital’s policies, Psychologists and patients must be located in New York State. Required Qualifications: MSW (foreign equivalent or higher) from an accredited Social Work Education School. New York State LCSW licensure. Knowledge and experience providing evidenced based psychotherapy including cognitive behavioral therapy, psychodynamic and insight-oriented therapies. Knowledge and experience in group therapy to adult patients who present with clinically complex symptoms and presentations. Preferred Qualifications: SIFI certified. Experience treating substance use disorder using evidence-based practices such as: CBT, Motivational Interviewing, Supportive-expressive Therapy, Relapse Prevention, Multi-dimensional Family Therapy, Contingency Management. Experience training social work interns. Experience providing care via telehealth videoconferencing platform. At least 3 years post licensure experience of conducting intake assessments, group therapy, and individual therapy. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Michele Chituk on email; Michele.Chituk@StonyBrookMedicine.edu. Special Notes: Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
