    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186989": {
      "title": "Nuclear Medicine Radiologist (Hybrid On-Site/Remote), Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Radiology, Nuclear Medicine",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Radiology Location: Stony Brook, New York Stony Brook Medicine Department of Radiology has an open position in Nuclear Medicine. Applicants are required to have either Residency in Nuclear Medicine or Diagnostic Radiology Residency with added competency in Nuclear Medicine or Fellowship in Nuclear Medicine. The Clinical Radiologist must be proficient in all aspects of Nuclear Medicine, PET Imaging and Theranostics. Title of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor and consideration of leadership position based upon qualifications. Flexible Schedule to include on-site and remote shifts in accordance with University policies. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: MD, DO (or foreign equivalent). NYS Licensure (eligible). Board Certified (eligible). Residency in Nuclear Medicine or Diagnostic Radiology Residency with added competency in Nuclear Medicine or Fellowship in Nuclear Medicine. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Training and Experience in all areas of Nuclear Medicine Radiology. Proficiency in Nuclear Medicine, PET Imaging and PET CT. Proficiency in Theranostics. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Elaine S. Gould MD, FACR at 631-444-5400. Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Technology and Management, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190303": {
      "title": "Interventional Radiologist, Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Radiology, Interventional",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Radiology Location: Stony Brook, New York The Radiology Department at Stony Brook University Hospital is seeking an Interventional Radiologist to join our growing team. The candidate will join a division of dedicated Interventional Radiologists, an IR Physician Assistant and an IR Nurse Practitioner. The candidate will perform a wide range of challenging and interesting procedures as Stony Brook is a Level 1 trauma center and the only tertiary care hospital in Suffolk County with a large referral base. They will also hold an academic appointment with our Renaissance School of Medicine with the opportunity to teach and mentor residents, fellows and medical students. Our Radiology Residency Program supports an ESIR Program, and we are considering beginning an Integrated IR Fellowship. There is also support for a Leadership position for qualified candidates as well as opportunities for research. Pur IR suite is located in the new hospital pavilion with state-of-the-art equipment, a dedicated IR CT and four (4) Angio rooms including a Bi-Plane room. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: MD, DO (or foreign equivalent). NYS Licensure (eligible). Board Certified (eligible) in Diagnostic Radiology. Fellowship training in Interventional Radiology at an ACGME-accredited institution. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Training and experience in all areas of VIR and Diagnositc Radiology. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfollio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Elaine S. Gould, MD FACR, Chair Department of Radiology, 631-444-5400. Special Notes: Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
