    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191250": {
      "title": "Pediatric Surgeon, Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Surgery, Pediatric",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Surgery Location: Stony Brook, New York The Division of Pediatric Surgery in the Department of Surgery at Stony Brook Medicine is seeking a board-certified/board-eligible pediatric surgeon to join our growing academic pediatric surgical program at Stony Brook Children’s Hospital. The successful candidate will be appointed at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor, or Clinical Professor, commensurate with experience and academic accomplishments. Stony Brook University Hospital is the region’s premier academic and tertiary care medical center, serving more than 1.5 million residents of Suffolk County and the surrounding region. Stony Brook Children’s Hospital opened its dedicated children’s hospital in 2019 and provides comprehensive pediatric and surgical specialty care in a modern, family-centered environment.  The hospital is the only ACS-verified Level I Pediatric Trauma Center in Suffolk County and includes a 46-bed Level III NICU with approximately 1,000 admissions annually. More than 180 pediatric specialists representing 30 specialties provide multidisciplinary care across the full spectrum of pediatric disease. The Division of Pediatric Surgery is committed to providing outstanding, compassionate, and evidence-based surgical care while advancing the academic missions of education, research, and innovation. The Division is supported by the Department of Surgery and Stony Brook Medicine, with opportunities for continued clinical program development, multidisciplinary collaboration, and regional growth. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will join an established pediatric surgery faculty and participate in the full range of clinical, educational, and scholarly activities of the Division. Responsibilities will include: Providing comprehensive operative and nonoperative care for infants, children, and adolescents with general and thoracic pediatric surgical conditions, including congenital anomalies, neonatal surgical disease, trauma, tumors, and other complex surgical conditions. Participating in inpatient, outpatient, operative, consultative, and call responsibilities of the Division. Working collaboratively with pediatric medical and surgical subspecialists, anesthesiologists, intensivists, neonatologists, nursing staff, advanced practice providers, and other members of the multidisciplinary pediatric care team. Participating in multidisciplinary conferences, quality-improvement initiatives, and programmatic efforts designed to improve pediatric surgical outcomes and access to care. Contributing to the continued growth and development of pediatric surgical services at Stony Brook Children’s Hospital and throughout the Stony Brook Medicine network. Teaching and mentoring medical students, general surgery residents, and other trainees in the operating room, inpatient and outpatient settings, conferences, and classroom. Academic Opportunity This position offers the opportunity to join a growing academic pediatric surgical program within a major university-based health system. The successful candidate will have opportunities to develop areas of clinical expertise, participate in multidisciplinary programs, contribute to research and education, and assume increasing academic or programmatic leadership responsibilities based on experience and interests. Faculty appointment and academic rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications, experience, and scholarly accomplishments. Required Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent medical degree. Completion of an accredited pediatric surgery fellowship or equivalent training. Board certification or board eligibility in Pediatric Surgery. Eligibility for medical licensure in the State of New York. Eligibility for DEA registration. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in pediatric surgical care, professionalism, teamwork, and education. Preferred Qualifications Strong academic credentials and demonstrated interest in medical education and mentorship. Experience in or demonstrated potential for clinical, translational, outcomes, health services, or educational research. Interest in program development, quality improvement, and multidisciplinary pediatric care. Additional clinical, research, educational, or leadership expertise that complements the existing strengths and future strategic priorities of the Division. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Tracey Maresco at 631-638-2326 Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193219": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant, Clinical Instructor, Surgery, Cardiothoracic Surgery (Inpatient Step Down Unit - Night Shift Position)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Surgery Location: Stony Brook, New York Join our esteemed healthcare team dedicated to providing exceptional care to our Cardiothoracic Surgery patients. We are seeking a dedicated Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant to join our dynamic team and contribute to our commitment to excellence in healthcare delivery. Schedule:  Full-time nights with ability to flex to alternate shifts based on the needs of the service. Weekends and holidays are required. Responsibilities: Patient Assessment and Care: Conduct thorough patient assessments, perform physical examinations, and formulate assessments and diagnoses. Initiate, review, and revise treatment plans, ensuring accurate documentation and presentation of data to the supervising physician. Medical Practice Support: Provide essential patient care services within the medical practice. Provide support and act as a resource to nursing staff. Direct inpatient pre and post op care of patients admitted to the cardiothoracic surgery service. Referrals and Consultations: Make referrals to other healthcare providers when necessary and consult with physicians for further definitive therapy. Collaborate with the healthcare team to ensure seamless patient care. Diagnostic Tests and Procedures: Order and evaluate appropriate diagnostic tests and procedures, maintaining a commitment to evidence-based practice. Patient Education: Instruct and counsel patients on healthcare, health maintenance, medical problems, treatment plans, nutrition, and related issues, ensuring a patient-centered approach. System Coordination: Facilitate efficient patient movement through the healthcare system and optimizing resource utilization through interdepartmental collaboration. Audits and Research Involvement: Participate in audits and research initiatives within the healthcare setting, contributing valuable insights and helping to advance our understanding and practices in Cardiothoracic surgical care. Additional Responsibilities: Perform any other duties as assigned by management, contributing to the overall success of the healthcare team. If you are a compassionate healthcare professional with a passion for Cardiothoracic Surgical care and meet the qualifications outlined below, we invite you to apply today. Join us in providing exceptional care and making a difference in the lives of our patients. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Nurse Practitioner: Master’s degree (foreign equivalent or higher) in Nursing or completion of a course for Nurse Practitioner and certification as a Nurse Practitioner in acute care, adult/gerontology, and/or family nurse practitioner. Current NYS RN license. One year experience as a NP in an acute care setting. Physician Assistant: NYS license and certification as a Physician Assistant. Bachelor’s degree (foreign equivalent or higher) from an accredited school of Physician Assistants. One year experience as a PA in an acute care setting. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Board certification. Experience working in a fast-paced medical practice. Experience in Cardiothoracic Surgery. Three years of experience as a NP/PA in an acute care setting. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Tracey Maresco at 631-638-2326 Special Notes: Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194211": {
      "title": "Advanced Otology Fellowship, Clinical Instructor, Surgery, Otolaryngology",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Surgery Location: Stony Brook, New York The Division of Otolaryngology at Stony Brook University Renaissance School of Medicine is seeking a qualified candidate for a one-year Advanced Otology Fellowship. This non-ACGME fellowship offers comprehensive training in advanced otologic and neurotologic surgery, preparing the fellow for independent practice and a competitive academic or private practice career in otology.  The fellow will be appointed at the rank of Clinical Instructor. The fellowship provides extensive surgical experience, including tympanoplasty, canal wall up and canal wall down mastoidectomy, stapes surgery, ossicular reconstruction, cochlear implantation, facial nerve decompression, lateral temporal bone resection, superior canal dehiscence repair, and cerebellopontine angle tumor surgery. Graduated autonomy is emphasized, with appropriate faculty supervision. The fellow will run two outpatient clinics weekly, participate in an attending-level call schedule, and manage a diverse otolaryngology patient population with a strong emphasis on otologic disease. Unlimited access to the temporal bone laboratory is provided, and the fellow will play an active role in resident education and temporal bone dissection teaching. Research and scholarly activity are strongly encouraged, with opportunities to publish and present at national and international meetings, including the American Otologic Society and American Neurotologic Society. The program follows all Stony Brook GME policies, including fatigue and wellness guidelines. Required Qualifications: MD or DO degree (or foreign equivalent) from an accredited medical school Successful completion of an ACGME-accredited Otolaryngology – Head and Neck Surgery residency Board eligible or board certified in Otolaryngology – Head and Neck Surgery Eligibility for New York State medical licensure Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Clinical Instructor at Stony Brook University Ability to participate in attending-level clinical duties, including outpatient clinics, operative cases, and call coverage Commitment to patient care, professionalism, and collaborative team-based practice Commitment to resident education and mentorship, including participation in temporal bone laboratory instruction Strong interpersonal and communication skills Preferred Qualifications: Interest in academic medicine, clinical research, and teaching Experience with or interest in scholarly activity, including publications or national presentations Career goals aligned with practice as a comprehensive otologist in academic or high-volume clinical settings All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Tracey Erickson at 631-638-3236. Special Notes Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192267": {
      "title": "Urologist, Clinical Assistant Professor, Urology, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Surgery",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Urology Location: Stony Brook, New York The Department of Urology is currently recruiting for a fellowship trained faculty member in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Surgery. This position is to provide patient care and education for medical students and residents, as well as develop and participate in clinical and/or laboratory research. Required Qualifications: M.D. degree, Board Certified or Eligible in Urology, academically oriented with demonstrated clinical, teaching and research ability. New York State Medical License or eligibility. Fellowship training in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Surgery. Preferred Qualifications: Competency in General Urology including Open, Laparoscopic and Robotic Surgery. Demonstrated clinical, teaching, and research abilities. Interest in Clinical Outcomes Research. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfollio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Cathy Sue Emerson at 631-444-3642. Special Notes: Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Technology and Management, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 603 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194418": {
      "title": "Vice Dean for Inclusive Excellence, Associate/Full Professor, Renaissance School of Medicine",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine Location: Stony Brook, New York The Renaissance School of Medicine (RSOM) at Stony Brook University is recruiting a Vice Dean of Inclusive Excellence.  This role will lead the implementation of the RSOM’s strategic plan on inclusive excellence, centralize and coordinate RSOM initiatives on inclusive excellence, train and develop RSOM faculty, staff and learners to meet goals in inclusive excellence, and cultivate external partnerships to support inclusive excellence. The selected candidate will have a faculty appointment in a RSOM department based on their area of expertise. Responsibilities: 1.  Lead Implementation of the RSOM’s Strategic Plan on Inclusive Excellence Lead efforts under the RSOM’s five-year strategic plan to infuse inclusive excellence into the School’s research, clinical and educational missions Promote the creation of a nurturing environment where all faculty, staff and learners can thrive, learn, conduct impactful research, and deliver outstanding patient care Monitor progress on the strategic plan and make adjustments as necessary to ensure success Support the well-being of all members of the RSOM community and promote a culture of respect Contribute to research and scholarship in inclusive excellence and health equity 2.  Centralize and Coordinate RSOM Initiatives on Inclusive Excellence Centralize and enhance the visibility of work being done at RSOM to promote inclusive excellence and health equity. Coordinate pathway and outreach programs to promote inclusive excellence Develop methods and metrics to assess RSOM climate and the effectiveness of programs and initiatives Strengthen holistic admissions and recruitment practices Lead committees charged with promoting inclusive excellence in undergraduate and graduate medical education and faculty affairs Develop RSOM policies and procedures that promote inclusive excellence Supervise administrative staff in overseeing the Office of Inclusive Excellence 3.  Train and Develop RSOM Faculty, Staff and Learners to Meet Goals in Inclusive Excellence Ensure that medical school curricula integrate content on health equity and social determinants of health Expand mentorship programs for students Support student-led programs and organizations that foster inclusive excellence and health equity Promote faculty development in inclusive teaching 4.  Cultivate External Partnerships to Support Inclusive Excellence Represent the RSOM in University and health system initiatives that impact inclusive excellence Work closely with the Chief Health Equity Officer and the Associate Dean for Admissions to advance initiatives on inclusive excellence and health equity Cultivate relationships with SUNY, AAMC, and other external organizations to promote inclusive excellence Partner with advancement and external agencies to obtain resources for training an inclusive workforce and conducting research on health equity Required Qualifications : M.D. (or equivalent medical degree) and/or Ph.D. in a relevant field of study. Ability to attain NYS License if MD and clinically active. A record of outstanding accomplishment in a discipline relevant to the academic mission of the Renaissance School of Medicine. Credentials and achievements that merit appointment as a professor or associate professor in the School of Medicine. Demonstrated experience and commitment to inclusive excellence and reducing health disparities. An in-depth understanding of issues and challenges facing a variety of student, faculty, staff, and community populations. Excellent leadership and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications : Experience in leading programs on inclusive excellence and/or health equity at the national level. Proven track record of leading with a data-informed approach and utilizing data to achieve successful outcomes. Experience leading culture change to support inclusive excellence. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Peter Igarashi, Knapp Endowed Dean at 631-638-2141. Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189481": {
      "title": "School of Nursing, Clinical Instructor/Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor (Family NP Program Director) (Non-Tenure Track, 0.80 - 1.0 FTE)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: School of Nursing Location: Stony Brook, New York Job Description: The Stony Brook University School of Nursing invites applications for a 0.8–1.0 FTE faculty appointment within our Graduate Program, along with the opportunity to serve as Program Director of the Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) program. This is an exceptional chance for an experienced Family Nurse Practitioner to play a key role in educating the next generation of advanced practice nurses while contributing to the continued development and growth of an established graduate program within a nationally recognized academic health center. We seek a dynamic clinician–educator with recent family practice experience who demonstrates excellence in advanced practice and a commitment to graduate nursing education. Candidates with experience precepting nurse practitioner students, teaching in upper division or graduate nursing programs, and/or serving in leadership or supervisory roles are strongly encouraged to apply. Faculty in the School of Nursing are part of a collaborative academic community committed to advancing health, preparing the next generation of nurse leaders, and improving healthcare through excellence in education, scholarship, and clinical practice. Program Direc tor Opportunity The selected candidate will also serve as Program Director for the Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) program, providing academic oversight and leadership for a program that prepares advanced practice nurses to deliver high-quality care to family practice. The Program Director reports to the Department Chair, with collaboration and consultation from the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and the Dean. In this role, the Program Director will: Provide leadership for the FNP curriculum and program outcomes Guide program evaluation and continuous improvement aligned with professional standards and accreditation expectations Ensure program quality and compliance with the School of Nursing Evaluation Plan and program benchmarks Collaborate with faculty, clinical partners, and school leadership to support student success and program development To support these responsibilities, dedicated workload support and an administrative stipend are provided for the duration of the Program Director appointment. Faculty Role and Impact As a Clinical Instructor, Clinical Assistant Professor, or Clinical Associate Professor, the successful candidate will contribute to the educational, scholarly, clinical, and community service missions of the School of Nursing.  Our clinical faculty lead innovative, student-centered teaching and experiential learning that prepares graduates with the advanced clinical reasoning, leadership, and practice competencies needed to thrive in today’s complex healthcare environment. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching and curriculum development within the Family Nurse Practitioner program and related graduate courses. Faculty members are encouraged to bring creativity and innovation to their teaching and are supported in advancing the Scholarship of Teaching and Learning, including the development, evaluation, and dissemination of innovative educational practices. Faculty appointed at the Clinical Assistant and Clinical Associate Professor levels are also expected to contribute to the broader mission of a major research-intensive university through scholarship, practice, and professional service. Opportunities to maintain clinical practice may be available, supporting continued engagement in family practice and strengthening the integration of clinical experience in teaching. Mentorship and Academic Community The successful candidate will mentor and inspire students as future nurse leaders while preparing them to deliver compassionate, culturally responsive, patient-centered care to individuals, families, and communities. Faculty are active members of a collegial academic community that values collaboration, mutual respect, and meaningful engagement across disciplines. The candidate will also help cultivate a supportive learning environment that welcomes varied perspectives and prepares graduates to provide high-quality care to diverse patient populations. Why Stony Brook? Stony Brook University is part of the State University of New York (SUNY) system and is a flagship public research institution located on Long Island, New York. The School of Nursing is closely affiliated with Stony Brook University Hospital and Stony Brook Medicine, providing rich opportunities for clinical collaboration, innovation, and interdisciplinary engagement. Faculty benefit from close collaboration with Stony Brook Medicine’s acute and critical care specialty services, offering valuable opportunities for clinical partnership, student placements, and continued engagement within a leading academic health system. Joining Stony Brook means becoming part of a vibrant academic community committed to excellence, discovery, and improving the health of the communities we serve. Rank and salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Applications should include a cover letter outlining current and previous teaching/practice experience and a CV. Applicants should be prepared to supply a list of no less than three references upon application and must successfully clear a criminal background check. About Stony Brook University School of Nursing Stony Brook University School of Nursing is a destination of choice recognized for excellence and innovation in education, leadership, research, advocacy, and practice within a supportive and inclusive environment. #1 Public University in New York State. Top 35 Public College in the US. Conveniently located 44 miles from New York City. Affiliation with a world class academic medical center. Ranked in the Top 10 for best online Masters Programs for the past 5 years. Stony Brook University is an R1 Research Institution. Stony Brook University is one of the two Flagship Universities in New York State. Top 10 University for diversity and internationalization. Stony Brook University School of Nursing NCLEX rates consistently above 90%. Required Qualifications: Valid Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) NYS and National Certification Valid NY State Professional Nurse License Recent Nurse Practitioner Experience in Family Practice Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral Degree (Earned or In Progress) Upper Division Teaching Experience Experience Precepting Nurse Practitioner Students Leadership/Supervisory Experience All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Angelea.Laccesaglia@stonybrook.edu , Business Administrator. Special Notes Non-Tenure track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Nursing ( School of Nursing's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: September 1, 2026 Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195204": {
      "title": "School of Nursing, Clinical Instructor/Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor (Pediatric Acute Care NP Program Director) (Non-Tenure Track, 0.80 - 1.0 FTE)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: School of Nursing Location: Stony Brook, New York The Stony Brook University School of Nursing invites applications for a 0.8–1.0 FTE academic year faculty appointment within our Graduate Program, with an additional opportunity to serve as Program Director of the Pediatric Acute Care Nurse Practitioner (PACNP) program. This is an exceptional chance for an experienced Pediatric Acute Care Nurse Practitioner to play a key role in educating the next generation of pediatric acute care providers while contributing to the continued development and growth of an established graduate program within a nationally recognized academic health center. Faculty in the School of Nursing are part of a collaborative academic community committed to advancing health, preparing the next generation of nurse leaders, and improving healthcare through excellence in education, scholarship, and clinical practice. Program Director Opportunity The selected candidate will serve as Program Director for the Pediatric Acute Care Nurse Practitioner (PACNP) program, providing academic oversight for a program that prepares advanced practice nurses to deliver high-quality care to acutely ill and critically ill pediatric populations. The Program Director reports to the Department Chair, with collaboration and consultation from the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and the Dean. In this role, the Program Director will: Provide leadership for the PACNP curriculum and program outcomes Guide program evaluation and continuous improvement aligned with professional standards and accreditation expectations Ensure program quality and compliance with the School of Nursing Evaluation Plan and program benchmarks Collaborate with faculty, clinical partners, and school leadership to support student success and program development To support these responsibilities, dedicated workload support and an administrative stipend are provided for the duration of the Program Director appointment. Faculty Role and Impact As a Clinical Instructor, Clinical Assistant Professor, or Clinical Associate Professor, the successful candidate will contribute to the educational, scholarly, clinical, and service missions of the School of Nursing. Our clinical faculty lead innovative, student-centered teaching and experiential learning that prepares graduates with the advanced clinical reasoning, leadership, and practice competencies needed to thrive in today’s complex healthcare environment. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching and curriculum development within the Pediatric Acute Care Nurse Practitioner program and related graduate courses. Faculty members are encouraged to bring creativity and innovation to their teaching and are supported in advancing the Scholarship of Teaching and Learning, including the development, evaluation, and dissemination of innovative educational practices. Faculty appointed at the Clinical Assistant and Clinical Associate Professor levels are also expected to contribute to the broader mission of a major research-intensive university through scholarship, practice, and professional service. Opportunities to maintain clinical practice may be available, supporting continued engagement in pediatric acute care and enhancing the connection between clinical practice and teaching. Mentorship and Academic Community The successful candidate will mentor and inspire students as future nurse leaders while preparing them to deliver compassionate, culturally responsive, patient-centered care to individuals, families, and communities. Faculty are active members of a collegial academic community that values collaboration, mutual respect, and meaningful engagement across disciplines. The candidate will also help cultivate a supportive learning environment that welcomes varied perspectives and prepares graduates to provide high-quality care to diverse patient populations. Why Stony Brook? Stony Brook University is part of the State University of New York (SUNY) system and is a flagship public research institution located on Long Island, New York. The School of Nursing is closely affiliated with Stony Brook University Hospital and Stony Brook Medicine, providing rich opportunities for clinical collaboration, innovation, and interdisciplinary engagement. Faculty benefit from close collaboration with Stony Brook Children’s Hospital and the pediatric specialty services of Stony Brook Medicine, providing exceptional opportunities for clinical partnership, student placements, and continued engagement in pediatric acute care within a leading academic health system. Joining Stony Brook means becoming part of a vibrant academic community committed to excellence, discovery, and improving the health of the communities we serve. About Stony Brook University School of Nursing Stony Brook University School of Nursing is a destination of choice recognized for excellence and innovation in education, leadership, research, advocacy, and practice within a supportive and inclusive environment. #1 Public University in New York State. Top 35 Public College in the US. Conveniently located 44 miles from New York City. Affiliation with a world class academic medical center. Ranked in the Top 10 for best online Masters Programs for the past 5 years. Stony Brook University is an R1 Research Institution. Stony Brook University is one of the two Flagship Universities in New York State. Top 10 University for diversity and internationalization. Stony Brook University School of Nursing NCLEX rates consistently above 90%. Rank and salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Required Qualifications: Valid Pediatric Acute-Care Nurse Practitioner NYS and National Certification (PACNP) Valid NY State Professional Nurse License Recent Nurse Practitioner Experience in Pediatric Acute Care Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral Degree (or foreign equivalent - Earned or In Progress) Experience Precepting Nurse Practitioner Students Upper Division Teaching Experience Leadership/Supervisory Experience All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Angelea.Laccesaglia@stonybrook.edu , Business Administrator. Special Notes: Non-Tenure track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Nursing ( School of Nursing's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: January 2027 Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine.  We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187632": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, School of Dental Medicine (Full-Time)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: School of Dental Medicine: Oral Biology and  Pathology Location: Stony Brook, New York The School of Dental Medicine (SDM) at Stony Brook University is seeking applications for a full-time, 12-month, tenure-track or tenured faculty appointment at the rank of assistant or associate professor in the Department of Oral Biology and Pathology, with dental biomaterials research expertise.  A tenure appointment requires tenure at present institution and qualifies for continuing appointment (tenure) under the Guidelines for Faculty Appointment and Promotions of the SDM. The successful candidate will contribute to the biomaterials curriculum for dental student and graduate programs; secure internal and external funding to support their research; demonstrate a continued record of scholarship; supervise dental student, resident and MS/PhD research projects and participate in school governance.  The position will focus on collaborating with clinicians in the laboratory assessment of different treatment protocols; creating and testing commercial products; and developing the next generation of dental biomaterials. The school is completing the construction and equipping of a dental biomaterials research lab for which this position will oversee.  It will be accessible to all departments in the SDM to engage in discipline-specific biomaterials research and provide opportunities for students and residents to conduct graduate level research projects. The SDM supports dental specialty residency programs in dental anesthesiology, endodontics, oral and maxillofacial radiology, orthodontics, pediatric dentistry, periodontics and prosthodontics, creating opportunities for biomaterials research that have potential cross-discipline collaborations.  Dental-centered research areas in the SDM include enamel and dentin bonding, dental materials, cell biology and microbiology, psychosocial aspects of health and illness, applications of cone-beam CT, dental implants, 3D printing and applications of artificial intelligence in dental imaging. Click here to learn more about Stony Brook's research faculty . Stony Brook University, the top-ranked public university in New York State, is an R1 university and member of the Association of American Universities, providing a highly interactive environment with extensive opportunities for collaborations with faculty and joint appointments in other schools/colleges on campus. Stony Brook University is a premier employer that provides exceptional rewards, including start-up packages in addition to medical, dental and vision benefits. The university's competitive salaries and benefits packages also include generous retirement plans, tuition assistance for employees, wellness initiatives and more.  For detailed information, visit the Stony Brook University website .  For more information about the School of Dental Medicine, visit dentistry.stonybrookmedicine.edu . Salary and academic rank are commensurate with qualifications. Required Qualifications: PhD degree (or foreign equivalent) in biomaterials science from a college or university program accredited by an agency recognized by the Council for Higher Education Accreditation (CHEA) Postdoctoral training Active NIH funding Evidence of collaborative biomaterials research Record of scholarship in relevant journals Teaching experience, within the last five years, of professional or graduate students Mentoring experience, within the last five years, of professional or graduate students Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience at a dental or medical school Experience serving on an NIH study section Engaged member of IADR/AADOCR Dental Material Interest Groups Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills A desire to create an environment that promotes collegiality All application materials must be submitted online.  Please use the Apply Now button to begin the application process. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site or contact its Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Erin Boccio, at (631) 632-3753 or erin.boccio@stonybrookmedicine.edu Special Notes Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position.  FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA.  To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Dental Medicine ( School of Dental Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care.  It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County.  With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center.  Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research.  Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine.  We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives.  We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187499": {
      "title": "Interventional Consultative Cardiologist, Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Internal Medicine, Cardiology, Southampton (184696)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: Southampton, New York The Heart Institute at Stony Brook Medicine is seeking an outstanding interventional and consultative cardiologist to help expand and shape cardiovascular services on the East End of Long Island. This is a unique opportunity where leadership in patient care, program development, and access to advanced services will have a direct and lasting impact on the community.  The successful applicant would: Play a leading role in the growth of a thriving general cardiology practice and interventional service in a region with expanding demand and rapid population growth. Provide independent STEMI call coverage at a full-service community hospital, supported by a dedicated cath lab team. Enjoy a balance of outpatient and inpatient cardiology clinical care responsibilities with opportunities to interpret echocardiograms, perform TEEs, and read cardiac imaging. Live and work in one of the most beautiful coastal communities in the Northeast, with quick access to beaches, vineyards, and waterfront living. Stony Brook Southampton Hospital (SBSH) is a vital part of the Stony Brook Medicine system, serving the East End of Long Island with a strong commitment to delivering outstanding, community-focused care anchored in the academic excellence of a world-class medical center. As a community-centered hospital, SBSH combines the personalized attention of a neighborhood institution with the resources, innovation, and expertise of a leading academic health system. Located in the heart of Southampton Village, SBSH has been consistently recognized as one of the region’s top workplaces by Newsday—a testament to its collegial culture and exceptional care. The South Fork is also home to the Shinnecock Nation, a self-governing, state-recognized Indigenous tribe, and offers unique connections to culture and community. Candidates should: Be board-certified/eligible in cardiovascular disease and Interventional Cardiology. Have at least 1–2 years of post-fellowship experience in independent PCI/STEMI call coverage. Be comfortable managing a high-volume general cardiology practice, including outpatient visits and noninvasive diagnostics. Collaborate within a highly collegial, team-based environment where communication and shared decision-making are valued. Desire to live on or near the South Fork or North Fork of Long Island to ensure close proximity (~20–30 minutes) to support timely STEMI call coverage. This is a rare opportunity to practice academic interventional cardiology while enjoying an outstanding quality of life in one of New York’s most scenic and vibrant regions with unparalleled access to ocean and bay beaches, boutique farms, vineyards, and charming waterfront towns. Enjoy year-round outdoor recreation—from biking and kayaking to fishing and hiking—as well as excellent public and private schools and family-friendly neighborhoods. The area offers pristine natural beauty with convenient access to New York City via the LIRR or ferry service from Montauk to Block Island, New London, or Martha’s Vineyard. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: MD, DO or MD/PhD (or foreign equivalent). Board Certified in Internal Medicine. Board certified/eligible in both Cardiovascular Disease and Interventional Cardiology. Excellence in clinical care and teaching in cardiology (inpatient and outpatient). U.S. work authorization. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Level II training in echocardiography or advanced imaging, including nuclear training. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Hal Skopicki at 631-444-1062. Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives: education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189162": {
      "title": "Cardiologist, Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Internal Medicine, Heart Failure (186949)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: Stony Brook, New York The Division of Cardiology at The Heart Institute, Stony Brook University Hospital, seeks a full-time academic Heart Failure/VAD cardiologist (Assistant or Associate or Full Professor levels) to join our expanding cardiovascular program. This position offers a robust and flexible mix of inpatient and outpatient clinical responsibilities within a major university-based Heart Institute. Clinical efforts, areas of focus, and academic activities will be tailored to align with individual strengths, subspecialty interests, and long-term career goals. This role also offers a complete academic commitment with support to establish or participate in translational, clinical, and/or basic science research. We are seeking a high-potential advanced heart failure/MCS cardiologist ready to grow into a key leadership role within a mature Joint Commission-certified program. You will be part of a collegial, innovative, nationally recognized and award-winning faculty committed to excellence in patient care, mentoring, and teaching. We serve a population of 1.7 million people in Suffolk County, with additional patients from the tri-state region. Stony Brook University Hospital has been ranked among the top 100 Hospitals for cardiac care by Healthgrades since 2016. Work alongside nationally recognized experts in advanced heart failure, VAD, MCS, CardioOncology and CardioObstetrics. The Heart Failure and Cardiomyopathy Center supports programs of excellence in cardio-oncology, adult congenital heart disease, cardio-obstetrics, sports cardiology and a second opinion program in advanced cardiac disease with award-winning programs in interventional, structural cardiology, and electrophysiology. Joint Commission-certified Heart Failure and Cardiomyopathy program (2013-present). Joint Commission-certified Mechanical Circulatory Assist Device program (2011-present). You will join a program with strong surgical partners, expanding referral base, and institutional backing to increase VAD, shock, and advanced HF volumes, with clear opportunities to shape program strategy. An individualized development plan will align your clinical focus (MCS, shock, transplant evaluation, cardio-oncology, imaging, outcomes research) with mentorship, leadership roles, and promotion criteria. Candidates will have access to tremendous division-supported infrastructure for clinical trials, outcomes research, and implementation science, with mentorship for early-career funding and support for national speaking and committee roles. Enjoy competitive academic salaries, productivity bonuses, a unique and comprehensive benefits package, loan forgiveness and extensive mentoring. Thrive in a supportive environment of excellence that prioritizes mentorship, sustainable work-life balance, leadership opportunities, and flexible, team-based scheduling to foster long-term career growth. Only a car or train ride away from New York City, Long Island offers a rich quality of life with family-friendly communities, award-winning schools, and vibrant communities including art and interest groups. Enjoy diverse neighborhoods, active outdoor activities year-round, running trails, water sports, and beautiful parks and beaches.  With its mix of suburban, urban, and rural lifestyles, Long Island is perfect for singles, couples, and families alike. Recent graduates (rising stars) from high-caliber training backgrounds and those seeking to elevate their current practice are encouraged to apply. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: The ideal candidate will be an ambitious and kind physician who enjoys seeing patients and is committed to contributing to the growth and long-term goals of the Heart Institute. MD, DO or MD/PhD (or foreign equivalent). Board certified in Internal Medicine and board eligible/board certified in Cardiovascular disease and/or Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology with expertise in heart failure and ventricular assist device management. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience and excellence in clinical subspecialty care, educational initiatives or cardiovascular research. We also particularly welcome early-career candidates from advanced heart failure/VAD fellowships who are ready to build a national profile in MCS, shock, or HF outcomes with strong institutional support. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Hal Skopicki at 631-444-1062. Special Notes: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine ( School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure ). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description: Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350.  It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189163": {
      "title": "Consultative and Non-Invasive Cardiologist, Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Internal Medicine, Cardiology, Southampton (186950)",
      "description": "Department: Stony Brook University: Health Sciences: Renaissance School of Medicine: Internal Medicine: Cardiology Location: Southampton, New York The Division of Cardiology at The Heart Institute, The Heart Institute at Stony Brook Medicine is seeking an outstanding Consultative and/or Non-Invasive Imaging cardiologist to help expand and shape cardiovascular services on the East End of Long Island. This is a unique opportunity where leadership in patient care, program development, and access to advanced services will have a direct and lasting impact on the community. You will be part of a warm, collegial, general cardiology practice committed to excellence in patient care in both outpatient and inpatient settings, with clear paths to local and system-wide leadership in care. This role offers opportunities in non-invasive imaging (echocardiograms, nuclear imaging, vascular imaging, CT etc.) to serve one of the most beautiful coastal communities in the Northeast against a population of 1.7 million people in Suffolk County. Stony Brook Southampton Hospital (SBSH) is a vital part of the Stony Brook Medicine system, serving the East End of Long Island with a strong commitment to delivering outstanding, community-focused care anchored in the academic excellence of a world-class medical center. As a community-centered hospital, SBSH combines the personalized attention of a neighborhood institution with the resources, innovation, and expertise of a leading academic health system. Provide high-quality ambulatory cardiovascular care within Heart Institute faculty practices, with a customized balance of urgent access clinic, longitudinal follow-up, and selected inpatient consultative responsibilities based on the candidate’s interests and expertise. Located in the heart of Southampton Village, SBSH has been consistently recognized as one of the region’s top workplaces by Newsday—a testament to its collegial culture and exceptional care. The South Fork is also home to the Shinnecock Nation, a self-governing, state-recognized Indigenous tribe, and offers unique connections to culture and community. Teach and mentor residents, APPs, and students in contemporary evaluation of hospital and practice based care with additional options to engage in quality improvement, clinical, outcomes or implementation science research based on the applicants career trajectory. Thrive in a supportive environment that prioritizes mentorship, sustainable work-life balance, leadership development, and team-based scheduling to foster long-term career growth. Enjoy extremely competitive salaries, productivity incentives, a comprehensive benefits package, eligibility for loan forgiveness programs, and structured mentoring for academic promotion. Only a car or train ride from New York City, Long Island offers outstanding quality of life, excellent schools, diverse communities, outdoor recreation, and vibrant cultural opportunities suitable for individuals and families. This role is ideal for early-career cardiologists from strong training programs who want meaningful autonomy, visible impact, but with direct mentorship and coaching within a major academic Heart Institute. It is also excellent for experienced cardiologists seeking to redesign their successful career while supporting real work-life balance. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: The ideal candidate will be an ambitious and kind physician who enjoys seeing patients, teaching and committed to contributing to the growth and long-term goals of the Heart Institute and being an invaluable member of the community. MD, DO or MD/PhD (or foreign equivalent). Board certified in Internal Medicine and board eligible/board certified in Cardiovascular Disease. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Certification (in echocardiography, cardiac CT/MRI, or related areas) will be based on the applicant’s desired trajectory. All application materials must be submitted online. Please use the Apply Now button to begin your application. For technical support, please visit Interfolio's Support Site ( https://support.interfolio.com/ ) or reach out to their Scholar Service Team at help@interfolio.com or (877) 997-8807. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Hal Skopicki at 631-444-1062. Special Notes Tenure/Non-Tenure Track position. FLSA Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA. To qualify for tenure and/or a senior faculty appointment, the candidate must meet the criteria established by the School of Medicine (School of Medicine's Criteria for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure). Anticipated Start Date: As soon as possible. Campus Description Long Island's premier academic medical center, Stony Brook Medicine, represents Stony Brook University's entire medical enterprise and integrates all of Stony Brook's health-related initiatives:  education, research and patient care. It encompasses Stony Brook University Hospital, Stony Brook Children's Hospital, the five Health Sciences schools -- Dental Medicine, Health Professions, Medicine, Nursing and Social Welfare -- as well as the major centers and institutes, programs and more than 50 community-based healthcare settings throughout Suffolk County. With 624 beds, Stony Brook University Hospital serves as Suffolk County's only tertiary care center and Regional Trauma Center. Stony Brook Children's, with more than 180 pediatric specialists in 30 specialties, offers the most advanced pediatric specialty care in the region. In the Medical and Research Translation (MART) building, two floors are occupied by Stony Brook University Cancer Center’s outpatient services, and four floors are devoted to cancer research. Diversity, equity and inclusion are essential core values at Stony Brook Medicine. We believe we do our best and most impactful work when we leverage our diverse, equitable and inclusive perspectives. We are proud to recruit and hire talented people from a wide variety of backgrounds and experiences. The selected candidate must successfully clear a background investigation. In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (631) 632- 6350. It can also be viewed online at the University Police website at http://www.stonybrook.edu/police ."
    },
